            0.743,
            0.744,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are many different kinds of rechargeable batteries that are used for different applications—from small "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "batteries used",
              "styles": [
                "underline"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.78,
            0.571,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in watches and phones to batteries used in laptops and tablet to bigger batteries that run inverters or drive electric vehicles (Fig. 4.10). However, rechargeable batteries also do not last forever. After being charged (Fig. 4.11) and used many times, they slowly wear out."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.587,
            0.792,
            0.809,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Oh, so this is the reason why after a year or two, the phone battery requires charging more often!"
            }
          ]
